@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] nix-toolchain-paths-in-action-keys
Every Nix tool MUST resolve through read_root_config("nix", name) at load
time so its store path is a target attribute and part of each consuming
action's key; a missing entry fails rather than falling back to PATH
(ADR-0269). The only exception is `tools/buck2 --no-nix`
(`[overalls] no_nix = true`), where the kit names its few tools by bare name,
every other tool fails at analysis, and only non_hermetic targets build.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] nix-rust-toolchain
nix_rust_toolchain MUST take rustc, rustdoc and clippy-driver only from the
`[nix] rust` store path, the single rust-overlay toolchain that
nix/rust-toolchain.nix defines, and nix_cxx_toolchain MUST link with the Nix
stdenv cc wrapper and binutils from `[nix] cc` and `[nix] bintools`, so a
Buck2 Rust binary links glibc and native libraries the way buildRustPackage
does and no tool resolves through PATH (ADR-0273, ADR-0269).
